Hi all,<div><br></div><div>I am hoping someone can offer a hint on writing what should be a simple function. From the nimble virtual workshop of <a href="https://htmlpreview.github.io/?https://github.com/nimble-training/nimble-virtual-2021/blob/master/overview.html" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://htmlpreview.github.io/?https://github.com/nimble-training/nimble-virtual-2021/blob/master/overview.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792476969201000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3OQA88Opg7FxrUOR9e4Ar3">2021</a>, at the end of section 5, there is an exercise to write a function for a vectorized dnorm. Below is some sample code for what I have so far, where if I set returnType(double(1)) I get an error from nimbleModel() about returnType, but if I use returnType(double(0)) it returns only the first entry of the vector (obviously). I am using nimble 0.12.1 and I should mention that I did not attend the workshop, so that may be part of the problem! Any suggestions would be greatly appreciated.</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Adrian</div><div><br></div><div>library(nimble)</div><div><br></div><div>code &lt;- nimbleCode({</div><div>  intercept ~ dnorm(0, sd = 1000)</div><div>  slope ~ dnorm(0, sd = 1000)</div><div>  sigma ~ dunif(0, 100)</div><div>  predicted.y[1:4]  &lt;- intercept + slope * x[1:4] # vectorized node</div><div>  y[1:4] ~ dnorm_vec(predicted.y[1:4], sd = sigma)</div><div>})</div><div><br></div><div><span style="white-space:pre">my_dnorm &lt;- nimbleFunction(
  run = function(x = double(1), 
                 mean = double(1), sd = double(0), 
                 log = logical(0, default = 0)) {
    returnType(double(1))
    logdens &lt;- dnorm(x, mean, sd, log = TRUE)
    if(log) return(logdens) else return(exp(logdens))
  })</span><br></div><div><span style="white-space:pre"><br></span></div><div><span style="white-space:pre">## Test (this works)</span></div><div><span style="white-space:pre">c_dnorm_vec &lt;- compileNimble(dnorm_vec)</span></div><div><span style="white-space:pre">c_dnorm_vec(1:10, mean = rep(2, 10), sd = 0.5, log = TRUE)</span></div><div><span style="white-space:pre"><br></span></div><div><span style="white-space:pre"># This returns an error about returnType</span></div><div><span style="white-space:pre">model &lt;- nimbleModel(code, inits = list(slope = rnorm(1), sigma = runif(1),</span></div><div><span style="white-space:pre">intercept = rnorm(1)), data = list(y = runif(4), x = runif(4)*10))</span></div><div><span style="white-space:pre"><br></span></div><div><br></div>
